---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="License — Strata">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="license-page">
      <h1>License</h1>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>AGPL-3.0-or-later</h2>
        <p>
          Strata is licensed under the <strong>GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later</strong> (AGPL-3.0-or-later). This is a copyleft license designed to ensure that the software and its derivatives remain free and open source.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>What AGPL Means</h2>
        <p>
          The AGPL is a strong copyleft license. Anyone who distributes Strata — whether as a compiled binary, bundled in a product, or as part of a service — must also distribute the complete corresponding source code under the same AGPL terms. Any modifications to the code must also be released under AGPL when distributed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>How AGPL Differs from GPL</h2>
        <p>
          The key difference between the AGPL and the standard GPL is the <strong>network use clause</strong>. The GPL's copyleft requirement triggers only when you <em>distribute</em> copies of the software. The AGPL adds that if you modify the software and run it on a network server — making it accessible over a network without distributing copies — you must still make the modified source code available to all users who interact with it over the network.
        </p>
        <p>
          This clause closes the "application service provider" loophole, ensuring that even web-based deployments contribute their improvements back to the community.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>What This Means for Users</h2>
        <p>
          As a user of Strata, you are free to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Use</strong> Strata for any purpose, personal or commercial</li>
          <li><strong>Modify</strong> the source code to suit your needs</li>
          <li><strong>Share</strong> copies with others</li>
          <li><strong>Study</strong> how the software works</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you distribute modified versions of Strata — whether as binaries, source code, or as a network service — those modifications must also be licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later. You must provide access to the complete modified source code.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>Contribution Implications</h2>
        <p>
          All contributions to Strata are accepted under the terms of AGPL-3.0-or-later. By submitting a pull request, patch, or any other contribution, you agree that your contribution is licensed under this license. Contributors retain copyright to their work but grant the project and its users a perpetual, irrevocable license to use, modify, and distribute that contribution under the AGPL.
        </p>
        <p>
          This ensures that the entire codebase — including community contributions — remains consistently licensed and free.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section">
        <h2>Attribution</h2>
        <p>
          Copyright 2024-2026 Strata Contributors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="license-section license-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Note:</strong> The <code>LICENSE</code> file containing the full AGPL-3.0-or-later text has not yet been added to the repository. It will be included in a future release. Until then, the official license text is available at the link below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="license-cta">
        <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html" class="btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Read the Official AGPL-3.0 Text
        </a>
        <a href="/about" class="btn-secondary">
          Back to About
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .license-page {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .license-page h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }

  .license-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .license-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }

  .license-section p {
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .license-section ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .license-section li {
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .license-section li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-teal-400);
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .license-section strong {
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }

  .license-section code {
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .license-note {
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-200);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .license-note p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .license-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-200);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .license-page h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .license-cta {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
